<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30383" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nardĭnus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νάρδινος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>made of nard, nard-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unguentum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					13, 1, 2, § 15</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nardĭ-num</span></b> ,
			i, n. (sc. vinum), <i>wine
				flavored with nard</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deprompsit nardini amphoram cellarius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil. 3, 2, 11</span></i>
			 Brix ad loc.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Resembling nard</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pira,</span>”
				<i>that smell like nard</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 15, 16, § 55</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
